Facebook OAuth flow was incomplete - auth initiation existed but callback handler was missing. Additionally, `upsertToken` attempted to insert `user_id` into a non-existent column.

## Changes

- **Added Facebook OAuth callback handler** (worker.js lines 100-102)
  - Token exchange via Facebook Graph API v18.0
  - Mirrors existing YouTube/TikTok callback pattern

- **Migration for user_id column** (0002_add_user_id_to_tokens.sql)
  - Adds `user_id TEXT` to tokens table
  - Required by existing `upsertToken` function

```javascript
// Before: only YouTube and TikTok handled
} else if (platform === "tiktok") {
  tokenUrl = "https://open.tiktokapis.com/v2/oauth/token/";
  body = new URLSearchParams({ ... });
}

// After: Facebook now handled
} else if (platform === "facebook") {
  tokenUrl = "https://graph.facebook.com/v18.0/oauth/access_token";
  body = new URLSearchParams({ code, client_id: env.FB_CLIENT_ID, 
    client_secret: env.FB_CLIENT_SECRET, redirect_uri: callbackUri });
}
```

All OAuth flows now use `${baseUrl}/api/auth/callback/${platform}` redirect URIs consistently and maintain user session via `folderId` parameter in post-auth redirect.

