The `setTimeout` calls in share button callbacks could set state on unmounted components, causing memory leaks.

**Changes:**
- Added `shareTimeoutRef` to store timeout IDs
- Added cleanup effect to clear timeout on unmount
- Clear existing timeout before setting new one to prevent multiple concurrent timeouts

```jsx
const shareTimeoutRef = useRef(null);

useEffect(() => {
  return () => {
    if (shareTimeoutRef.current) {
      clearTimeout(shareTimeoutRef.current);
    }
  };
}, []);

// In callbacks:
if (shareTimeoutRef.current) {
  clearTimeout(shareTimeoutRef.current);
}
shareTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => setShareStatus({ type: null, message: "" }), 3000);
```

